 "description": "Update an authored component's complete version-4 source/metadata IN PLACE (same id) \u2014 the correct verb for the author\u2192preview\u2192fix loop (preview_component returns the admission or runtime error; fix the template here and re-preview, instead of creating a new component each iteration). Pass componentId + the changed fields as `body`. Same source contract as create_component: {version:4, componentId, template, manifest, definition}, admitted before the write; the template finds its root with document.getElementById('root'), and declared slots arrive in the scene's `assets`, never params. PLACED CLIPS: every placed clip renders the exact version it pins, so an update moves placed clips ONLY when you name a project \u2014 put `projectId` (and optionally `compositionId`; default the project's active composition) in `body`, and that composition's placements move to the new version in the same write. The answer carries `repinned` (what moved) and `placementsPinnedToPrevious` (placements across the org still rendering the previous version). Without `projectId` nothing placed moves: previews and renders of an existing clip keep the old version. For one placement, register the source WITHOUT projectId, read its immutable sourceVersionId, then use apply_composition clip.update to change only the selected clip source and exact pin under observed concurrency expectations. Explicit-project update_component admits and repins all matching placements in that composition; use it only when that broader edit is requested.",
